# Mix: a double tap on a track's black key solos it and the solo stays, let go (any page); a tap ends it and the
# mutes come back. A hold still adds a track while held; a mute changed elsewhere ends the solo first
wait 300
tap GLO
expect mute 0
tapkey b2
wait 100
tapkey b2
wait 40
expect mute 1019
wait 1200
expect mute 1019
shot mix_solo_latched.png
# a hold adds track 4 while held; let go, track 2 still alone
key b4 down
wait 900
expect mute 1003
key b4 up
wait 40
expect mute 1019
# a tap: the solo ends
tapkey b5
wait 400
expect mute 0
# track 1 muted, then track 3 double tapped: the first tap's mute undone, track 1's kept to go back to
tapkey b1
wait 400
expect mute 2
tapkey b3
wait 100
tapkey b3
wait 40
expect mute 1015
# another track double tapped while soloed: it alone
tapkey b6
wait 100
tapkey b6
wait 40
expect mute 959
tapkey b6
wait 400
expect mute 2
# a muted track still shows its steps on its meter, in grey (an empty muted track none)
notes 2 1 1 1 100 60
notes 2 1 5 1 100 62
notes 2 1 9 1 100 64
notes 2 1 13 1 100 65
tap PLAY
wait 600
expect mute 2
tapkey b3
wait 900
expect mute 10
shot mix_muted_meter.png
tap PLAY
